            "review_title": "Review at An Com Uong Nuoc Thai Bistro & Coffee - Kin Khao Kin Nam",
            "review_text": "Lolad93\nMelbourne, Victoria, Australia11 contributions\n0\nA ‘mehhh’ kinda place\nJul 2019 • Solo\nI came to the restaurant around 1pm (late lunch hours for a Viet), and ordered fried rice w/ egg & shrimp and a clear tom yum soup. Now, if you’re curious about this place and want to go here for an IG post, go for it. BUT if you’re here to eat, you’re in for an experience.\n\nThe food was ok, not great nor bad. I did have to wait 20mins for my fried rice and 30mins for my tom yum. The fried rice was quite typical, plus the soft boil egg, nothing “special”. There were 1 shrimp, 4-5 pieces of oyster mushrooms & some other herbs for flavour. NOT worth the wait. I sat at the table for 5mins, with my fried rice and waiters walking pass multiple times (including one cleaning the other end of my shared table), before they brought out the cutlery. During my lunch, 3 tables cancelled their orders because of the long waiting time. Also, I heard at least a dozen times of ‘excuse the restaurant because it’s a busy time’ or ‘sorry, we run out of food’. For a place with an advertised opening hour of between 9am - 10:30pm, those weren’t (and should never be) acceptable excuses.\n\nBottom line is: Don’t waste your time here 🤷🏻‍♂️\nRead more\nWritten July 28, 2019",
